<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Pálava: Děvičky–Děvín–Sirotčí hrádek — Dolní Věstonice, Děvičky, Děvín and Sirotčí hrádek complete loop [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>Walk the full clockwise circuit from Dolní Věstonice through Děvičky castle visitor ground, the Děvín ridge and current marked viewpoint approach, then the southern and southeast Sirotčí hrádek visitor forecourt before returning to Dolní Věstonice. Retain both castles and the ridge; use the current marked network and designated castle paths, with each selected visitor spur returning along the same path. The complete course is approximately 15.8 km.

Stay on the marked walking network and specifically admitted castle visitor footpaths; respect barriers and admission/opening at Děvičky. No interior climbing or unsafe masonry is included.

Sirotčí hrádek is approached from the south through the southeast visitor forecourt and returned the same way. The northern approach is excluded. Do not shortcut protected steppe or trample vegetation.

Limestone, rocky paths, steps and exposed cliffs become slippery in rain, snow or ice. Prefer dry, snow-free daylight; wind, summer heat and ordinary village-road traffic require care.

Obey current manager notices, signs, barriers and lawful restrictions. The complete two-castle ridge circuit is unavailable if any required leg is prohibited, closed or unsafe.

Inherited 659 m ascent and descent and six hours are approximate planning estimates without a measured elevation profile; allow extra time for conditions and castle visits.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 — https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright; https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/. Source: https://api.openstreetmap.org/api/0.6/map?bbox=16.627,48.84,16.669,48.893. Changes: ordered original source nodes and literal way segments, reversing actual segments for returns; duplicate shared junction nodes removed where needed. Canonical display uses the repository’s deterministic simplification of existing source vertices; the complete default variant and research GPX retain every literal source edge. No synthetic connectors, private guide/map coordinates or elevations. Two-dimensional planning geometry; not navigation-grade or legal permission.

